' Watchfire autostart, run from the Windows Startup folder at logon.
' Rendered by deploy/install.sh (which fills in the WSL distro name) — edit the
' template deploy/watchfire-boot.vbs.in, then re-run the installer.
'
' The catch: Startup fires at logon, often BEFORE the WSL service (LxssManager)
' is ready — so a single wsl.exe call fails silently and the widget never opens
' (the server still comes up later via systemd when WSL boots for another
' reason, but the widget doesn't). So: retry a trivial wsl.exe until WSL answers
' (which also boots the distro -> systemd + linger start the server), then hand
' off to boot-widget.sh, which waits for :4173 and opens the widget window.
'
' Run(cmd, 0, True)  = hidden window, wait, return exit code.
' Run(cmd, 0, False) = hidden window, don't wait (fire-and-forget).
Set sh = CreateObject("WScript.Shell")

n = 0
Do
    If sh.Run("wsl.exe -d @DISTRO@ -- /bin/true", 0, True) = 0 Then Exit Do
    n = n + 1
    WScript.Sleep 5000            ' WSL not ready yet — wait and retry (cap ~5 min)
Loop While n < 60

sh.Run "wsl.exe -d @DISTRO@ -- bash -lc ""~/.watchfire/boot-widget.sh""", 0, False
